// "Unless" — the ENGLISH ORDER over the collapsed `May(Pay(cost))` MustPay
// shape ([CR#118.12a] — the CR itself defines the punisher as
// `May`-without-`if_did`): "[effect] unless [who] pays [cost]" is
// `May { who, effect: Pay(cost), if_not: effect }`, exactly. Core keeps only
// the `May` node; this macro is the render name the corpus's unless-order
// spellings (Mana Leak's "counter target spell unless its controller pays
// {3}", the upkeep-toll "sacrifice ~ unless you pay …") read and write
// through — the parser's counter/sacrifice emitters keep emitting
// `Unless(...)` invocations, which expand to `May(Pay(...))` at read time.
//
// Rendering rides the structural `May` arm (which conjugates the payer
// verb — "unless you pay" / "unless its controller pays"); the template
// documents the surface order.
(
    name: "Unless",
    template: "${effect} unless ${who} pays ${unless}",
    kinds: [OneShotEffect],
    params: { "effect": OneShotEffect, "who": Default(Reference, You), "unless": Cost },
    body: May(
        who: Param(who),
        effect: Pay([Splice(Param(unless))]),
        if_not: Param(effect),
    ),
)
